A||N||4||AusFiero||SNOW ??? It doesn't snow here||||1||
Z||000000||AusFiero||08-27-2001||06:36 PM||||Well our weather has been crazy lately. Been battling huge winds that have been doing a lot of damage. My shed is dead. Then we get massive rain storms. Followed by rain and huge winds. Well yesterday was the day to top them all. 15 minutes drive from my place it snowed. 3rd time in my lifetime and the heaviest falls in known history for the area.<BR>The picture below does not do the storm justice as this was hours after the snowfall and it melts pretty quickly here. Particularly with the rain that followed.<P>Anybody elses weather patterns seem crazy?<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/snow.jpg"> <BR><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000001||rodmcneill||08-27-2001||06:45 PM||||What did the kids think of the snow?||||reg||5
Z||000002||Urchin||08-27-2001||07:14 PM||||Temperature fluctuations as well, or just winds and parcipitation?  I have never been to Australia, I was always under the impression it didn't get cold enough there for snow.  <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/side_cut_sig_4.jpg">  <BR>If you can read this, I'm parked.||||reg||1
Z||000003||AusFiero||08-27-2001||07:51 PM||||The eldest kid (5) loved it. She had a ball. The son (2.5) got back in the car as quick as he could. Obviously going to be a beach loving stuff this snow stuff man.<P>Yeah it gets cold enough to snow here. Particularly in the Snowy Mountains NSW and the Victorian alps. Both are about 4 to 5 hours drive away. That is our skiing part of the country. But to snow here is rare. Very rare. It snowed when I was 5 again when I was 17 and now at 35 it has hit big time. As I said the photo does not do it justice as that was hours later and it had been raining heavily for a fair while.  The wierd thing is the day before it was hot and summer like. Except for the winds. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Phil||08-27-2001||09:45 PM||||Cheer up Spring is coming.||||reg||1
